{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#255","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#255","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#255\",\"parent_revision\":\"586356f1e9bf0e546414723d0baf69d284da93fd\",\"root_revision\":\"55e2941be6dad97370a8875ea7ca1d59e901b009728a4c1dd5601a9b5707807a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWrap `validate_glfm.py` and `sync_gitlab_docs.py` as MCP tools. Agents could validate GitLab Flavored Markdown compliance and sync documentation without shell access. Tools: `validate_glfm`, `sync_docs`, `list_glfm_errors`.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `validate_glfm.py` exists in gitlab-skill plugin | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/gitlab-skill/scripts/` |\\n| 2 | `sync_gitlab_docs.py` exists in gitlab-skill plugin | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/gitlab-skill/scripts/` |\\n| 3 | gitlab-skill plugin has MCP infrastructure or can add it | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/gitlab-skill/.mcp.json` and `plugin.json` |\\n| 4 | FastMCP patterns for PEP 723 scripts established | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` as reference |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information derivable from codebase inspection.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **gitlab-skill: gitlab ci & glfm validation mcp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: MCP backlog audit 2026-02-23\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Location\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/gitlab-skill/mcp/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Docs. Adds MCP capability to gitlab-skill. No changes to existing scripts. Low risk \u2014 additive only.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- MCP tool `validate_glfm` wraps `validate_glfm.py`; accepts a file path or markdown string, returns list of GLFM violations\\n- MCP tool `sync_docs` wraps `sync_gitlab_docs.py`; accepts source and destination parameters, returns sync summary\\n- MCP tool `list_glfm_errors` returns structured error objects from a previous validation run\\n- All three tools registered in `plugins/gitlab-skill/.mcp.json`\\n- FastMCP server validated with `uv run fastmcp list`\\n- Tools appear in an active session when the gitlab-skill plugin is installed\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/gitlab-skill/scripts/validate_glfm.py` \u2014 script to wrap\\n- `plugins/gitlab-skill/scripts/sync_gitlab_docs.py` \u2014 script to wrap\\n- `plugins/gitlab-skill/scripts/run_mcp_server.py` \u2014 new MCP server (PEP 723, FastMCP)\\n- `plugins/gitlab-skill/.mcp.json` \u2014 MCP server registration\\n- `plugins/gitlab-skill/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version bump\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent using the gitlab-skill plugin, I need `validate_glfm.py` and `sync_gitlab_docs.py` exposed as MCP tools so I can validate GitLab Flavored Markdown compliance and sync documentation without shell access.\\n\",\"digest\":\"7080c113010463d9991f04c7f44eea63d49da2196b5b0dc7606156f8c05cc9a0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg15RA\"}"}